## The eq call site: generated helpers reach the wire, and a pattern defect they hid

`rust-codex-compiler` `5a98dee`, over `9900fad`. Subject and oracles unchanged
at `8570fba1`.

### What was built

`lower-eq-dispatch`. `==` and `/=` on a type the desugarer generated
`__eq_<T>` for become a call to it; the arm probes the overlay and then the
checker's bindings for the NAME, which is upstream's `lookup-type-split`, and
finding it is the whole proof the operand is such a type. A type with
arguments is called by the instantiated name, `__eq_Box@Integer`, which
`codexir` puts on the wire with no definition attached. `/=` is
`if call then False else True`. A list has no helper and stays `binary eq`.

Before this every generated helper was dead: emitted, named by nothing,
pruned. The self-host oracle names `__eq_TokenKind` sixteen times; we named it
zero.

### The defect the dead helpers hid

Every pattern in a generated definition carries the same synthetic span. Our
checker recorded a pattern type per span, so all of them shared one key and
`pat_type_at` answered the FIRST helper's type for every derived pattern:
`Red` in `__eq_Color` came back as `Tup2`, the prelude's first helper. Nothing
saw it while the helpers were pruned. The checker now skips a synthetic span,
as it already did for expression types, and lowering rebuilds a sub-pattern's
type from the constructor's binding and the scrutinee -- upstream's
`resolved-ctor-field-type`, which it does for every pattern.

This is the anti-pattern Steve named this morning, in both directions. Upstream
does not carry forward WHICH types the desugarer gave helpers, so lowering
infers it from a string probe of the type environment and re-derives the
instance key from the resolved operand. Our `pat_types` tried to carry the
checker's knowledge forward, but keyed by span, and the desugarer's synthetic
span is not an identity -- so the carried knowledge was lossy exactly where it
was needed and we fell back to the same reconstruction. The honest fix
upstream of both is a node identity the desugarer mints, which no layer has.

### Measured before the gates

Two probes against `codexir`: a nullary sum, a generic sum at a concrete and at
a variable argument, a list, and a sum with a generic-sum field. Byte-identical
on the BUNDLED source, all six definitions; on the raw source one type-variable
number differs because our `irdump` bundles the prelude and `codexir` reads
stdin. 219 tests, one new, pinning that wire.

Survey of the oracle wire over all 1,269 units, banked as
`eq-helper-sites-on-oracle-wire.tsv` beside the run: **10 units name a helper**
-- 8 the plain name, 2 also an instantiated one. So this arm can move at most
about ten units on the corpus IR gate; the self-host is where it shows.

### Predictions, registered before the run

    self-host wire     MISSING 1 -> 0; identical up from 2,714 of 2,869
    corpus IR          identical up by 3-10 from 879; refusal rows unchanged
    corpus counters    EXACTLY 984 agree / 68 diverge -- nothing counted moved
    corpus diag        unchanged

Run: `~/runs/rustarm-20260909T124555Z-eqsite/` -- `gates.sh` does release
build, self-host, corpus IR, corpus counters; `after.sh` appends the
