## The 33-unit family was one span: `map-list` carries the loop variable's

Run 1's controls held exactly -- counters 984/68, diagnostics 1096/173 -- and
run 2's self-host equals run 1's to the definition (2,729 of 2,869, MISSING 0,
the same 140 DIFFERS). Run 2 continues on the corpus gates.

While it ran, the family. `tools/mintprofile.sh` on `list-comprehension-copy`
was no use: its "ours" column read zero expr-types on every prefix. The cause
is the tool, not the checker -- a truncated prefix of a RESOLVED unit loses a
cited chapter, `bundle::load` sees it missing and re-resolves against the
ambient `CODEX_ROOT`, which is on another branch. The tool pre-dates resolved
units. Left as is and recorded here; `tools/README.md` should say it before
anyone else reaches for it.

The answer came from reading upstream's `ForExpr` arm instead. It stamps the
invented `map-list` NAME with `token-span var-tok`, the loop variable's real
span; only the lambda and the two applications are synthetic. Ours stamped all
four synthetic, so the checker recorded nothing for the name: one `expr-types`
short per comprehension, which is exactly the family's shape -- `ai-*` short by
8 to 11, `list-comprehension-copy` by 1.

`1354fec` gives the name the variable's span. Measured with the debug binaries
before any gate:

    the 33 family units    33 agree on all four counters, 0 diverge
    self-host counters     EXACT on all four; expr-types 147,916 = the oracle
                           (the +216 residual was the compiler's comprehensions)
    list-comprehension-copy wire   DIFFERS 4 lines in run 1 -> byte-identical

This is the anti-pattern's mirror image: upstream DID carry knowledge forward
from the parser -- a real position onto a node the desugarer invents -- and
the port dropped it on the assumption that invented means synthetic. The
lowering comment that reasoned from that assumption is corrected in the commit after `1354fec`.

Run 3 is queued behind run 2 as `~/runs/rustarm-20260909T132000Z-maplist-span/`
(its header carries two stray lines from a sed over run 2's script; the
PURPOSE and prediction lines are right). Predictions: corpus counters
