safari-codex named its own language worktree in pins.tsv
(`cobblestone ~/showell_repos/cobblestone-safari`), sitting at `422405d0`
(Update 55 era) while codexzig and codexwasm had both moved to `8570fba1` (the
u58 candidate). A second copy of a pin the transpilers already carry is the
copy that drifts; the arms would have graded a U55 language with U57 binaries
and nothing said so. Steve's call: the private-pin mechanism dated to the
earliest days and was never anything but a footgun -- remove it.

`harness/cobblestone_pin.py` now derives the checkout from the two borrowed
transpilers' generated provenance and REFUSES if they disagree -- the agreement
is the drift check at the one place it matters. pins.py, spec/run.sh and
